INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Weighted Ball Hyperextension', 'Bas du dos', 'Swiss ball', '1. To begin, lie down on an exercise ball with your torse pressing against the ball and parallèle au sol. The ball of vos pieds should be pressed against le sol to help keep you balanced. Place a weighted plate under your chin or behind your neck. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Lentement, raise your torse up by bending at the waist and lower back. Remember to expirez during this movement.
3. Hold the contraction on your lower back for a second and lower your torse back down to the position de départ while inhaling.
4. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité. prescribed in your program.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Milieu du dos. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Weighted_Ball_Hyperextension/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Weighted Ball Side Bend', 'Abdominaux', 'Swiss ball', '1. To begin, lie down on an exercise ball with your left side of the torse (waist, hanches and épaule) pressed against the ball.
2. vos pieds should be on le sol while vos jambes are crossed and hanging from the ball. Hold a weighted plate with your right hand directly to the right side of votre tête. Conseil : Make sure the smooth side of the plate is resting against votre tête.
3. Place your left arm across your torse so that your palm is on your obliques. There should be a right angle between your left forearm and upper arm. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Raise the side of your torse up by laterally flexing at the waist while exhaling.
5. Hold the contraction for a second and Lentement, lower yourself back down to the position de départ while inhaling.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.
7. Switch sides and Répétez the exercise.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Weighted_Ball_Side_Bend/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Weighted Bench Dip', 'Triceps', 'Autre', '1. For cet exercice you will need to place a banc behind votre dos and another one in front of you. With the benches perpendiculaire à votre corps, hold on to one banc on its edge with the hands close to votre corps, separated at épaule width. vos bras should be fully extended.
2. The legs will be extended forward on top of the other banc. vos jambes should be parallèle au sol while your torse is to be perpendiculaire à le sol. Have your partner place the haltère on your lap. Note: cet exercice is best performed with a partner as placing the poids on your lap can be challenging and cause injury without assistance. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Lentement, lower votre corps as you inspirez by bending at the coudes until you lower yourself far enough to where there is an angle slightly smaller than 90 degrees between the upper arm and the forearm. Conseil : Keep the coudes as close as possible throughout le mouvement. Forearms should always be pointing down.
4. Using your triceps to bring your torse up again, lift yourself back to the position de départ while exhaling.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Pectoraux, Épaules. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Weighted_Bench_Dip/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Weighted Crunches', 'Abdominaux', 'Medecine ball', '1. Allongez-vous au sol with vos pieds flat on the ground or resting on a banc with your genous bent at a angle de 90 degrés.
2. Hold a poids to your poitrine, or you may hold it extended above your torse. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Now, expirez and Lentement, begin to roll your épaules off le sol. Your épaules should come up off le sol about 4 inches while your lower back remains on le sol.
4. At the top of le mouvement, flex your abdominals and hold for a brief pause.
5. Then inspirez and Lentement, lower yourself back down to the position de départ.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Weighted_Crunches/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Weighted Jump Squat', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. Position a lightly loaded barre across the back of your épaules. You could also use a weighted vest, sandbag, or other type of resistance for cet exercice.
2. The poids should be light enough that it doesn''t slow you down significantly. vos pieds should be just outside of épaule width with votre tête and poitrine up. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Using a countermovement, squat partially down and immediately reverse your direction to explode off of the ground, extending through your hanches, genous, and chevilles. Maintain good posture throughout the jump.
4. As you return to the ground, absorb the impact through vos jambes.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Weighted_Jump_Squat/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Weighted Pull Ups', 'Dos', 'Autre', '1. Attach a poids to a dip belt and secure it around your waist. Grab the pull-up bar with the paumes vers l''avant. For a prise moyenne, vos mains should be spaced at épaule width. Both arms should be extended in front of you holding the bar at the chosen grip.
2. You''ll want to bring your torse back about 30 degrees while creating a curvature in your lower back and sticking your poitrine out. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Now, expirez and pull your torse up until votre tête is above vos mains. Concentrate on squeezing yourshoulder blades back and down as you reach the top contracted position.
4. After a brief moment at the top contracted position, inspirez and Lentement, lower your torse back to the position de départ with vos bras extended and your lats fully stretched.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Milieu du dos. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Weighted_Pull_Ups/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Weighted Sissy Squat', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. Standing upright, with feet at épaule width and toes raised, use one hand to hold onto the beams of a squat rack and the opposite arm to hold a plate on top of your poitrine. C''est votre position de départ.
2. As you use one arm to hold yourself, bend at the genous and Lentement, lower your torse toward the ground by bringing your pelvis and genous forward. Inspirez as you go down and stop when your upper and lower legs almost create a angle de 90 degrés. Hold the stretch position for a second.
3. After your one second hold, use your cuisse muscles to bring your torse back up to the position de départ. Expirez as you move up.
4. Répétez for the recommended amount of times.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Avancé.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Weighted_Sissy_Squat/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Weighted Sit-Ups - With Bands', 'Abdominaux', 'Autre', '1. Start out by strapping the bands around the base of the decline banc. Place the handles towards the inside of the decline banc so that when lying down, you can reach for both of them.
2. Position vos jambes through the decline machine until they are secured. Now reach for the exercise bands with both hands. Use a pronated (palms forward) grip to grasp the handles. Position them near your collar bone and rotate your poignet to a neutral grip (paumes vers the torse). Note: vos bras should remain stationary throughout the exercise. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Move your torse upward until your upper body is perpendiculaire à le sol while exhaling. Hold the contraction for a second and lower your upper body back down to the position de départ while inhaling.
4. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Weighted_Sit-Ups_-_With_Bands/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Weighted Squat', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. Start by positioning two flat benches épaule width apart from each other. Stand on top of them and wrap the weighted belt around your waist with the amount of poids you feel comfortable with. Make sure your toes are facing out.
2. Once you are standing straight up with the poids hanging in between vos jambes, position vos bras so that they are fully extended to the side of votre corps. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Begin by bending the genous as you maintain a straight posture with the head up. Continue down until the angle between the upper leg and the mollets becomes slightly less than 90-degrees (which is the point in which the upper legs are below parallèle au sol). Inspirez as you perform this portion of le mouvement. Conseil : If you performed the exercise correctly, the front of the genous should make an imaginary straight line with the toes that are perpendiculaire à the front. If your genous are past that imaginary line (if they are past your toes) then you are placing undue stress on the genou and the exercise has been performed incorrectly.
4. Begin to move the body back up by pushing le sol of the flat banc with the ball of your foot mainly as you straighten the legs again and go back to the position de départ. Expirez as you perform this portion of the exercise.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Weighted_Squat/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Wide-Grip Barbell Bench Press', 'Pectoraux', 'Barre', '1. Allongez-vous au sol on a flat banc with feet firm on le sol. Using a wide, pronated (palms forward) grip that is around 3 inches away from épaule width (for each hand), lift the bar from the rack and hold it straight over you with vos bras locked. The bar will be perpendiculaire à the torse and le sol. C''est votre position de départ.
2. As you Inspirez, come down Lentement, until you feel the bar on your middle poitrine.
3. Après une pause, bring the bar back to the position de départ as you Expirez and push the bar using your poitrine muscles. Lock vos bras and squeeze your poitrine in the contracted position, Maintenez la position 1 seconde and then start coming down Lentement, again. Conseil : It should take at least twice as long to go down than to come up.
4. Répétez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Wide-Grip_Barbell_Bench_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Wide-Grip Decline Barbell Bench Press', 'Pectoraux', 'Barre', '1. Allongez-vous au sol on a decline banc with the feet securely locked at the front of the banc. Using a wide, pronated (palms forward) grip that is around 3 inches away from épaule width (for each hand), lift the bar from the rack and hold it straight over you with vos bras locked. The bar will be perpendiculaire à the torse and le sol. C''est votre position de départ.
2. As you Inspirez, come down Lentement, until you feel the bar on your lower poitrine.
3. Après une pause, bring the bar back to the position de départ as you Expirez and push the bar using your poitrine muscles. Lock vos bras and squeeze your poitrine in the contracted position, Maintenez la position 1 seconde and then start coming down Lentement, again. Conseil : It should take at least twice as long to go down than to come up.
4. Répétez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Wide-Grip_Decline_Barbell_Bench_Press/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Wide-Grip Decline Barbell Pullover', 'Pectoraux', 'Barre', '1. Allongez-vous sur un banc décliné with both legs securely locked in position. Reach for the barre behind the head using a pronated grip (paumes vers out). Make sure to grab the barre wider than épaule width apart for cet exercice. Lentement, lift the barre up from le sol by using vos bras.
2. When positioned properly, vos bras should be fully extended and perpendiculaire à le sol. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Begin by moving the barre back down in a semicircular motion as if you were going to place it on le sol, but instead, stop when the arms are parallèle au sol. Conseil : Keep the arms fully extended en permanence. le mouvement should only happen at the épaule joint. Inspirez as you perform this portion of le mouvement.
4. Now bring the barre up while exhaling until you are back at the position de départ. Remember to keep full control of the barre en permanence.
5. Répétez le mouvement for the prescribed amount of repetitions of your training program.
6. When finished with your set, Lentement, lower the barre back down until it is level with votre tête and release it.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules, Triceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Wide-Grip_Decline_Barbell_Pullover/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Wide-Grip Lat Pulldown', 'Dos', 'Poulie', '1. Sit down on a pull-down machine with a wide bar attached to the top pulley. Make sure that you adjust the genou pad of the machine to fit your height. These pads will prevent votre corps from being raised by the resistance attached to the bar.
2. Grab the bar with the paumes vers l''avant using the prescribed grip. Note on grips: For a prise large, vos mains need to be spaced out at a distance wider than épaule width. For a prise moyenne, vos mains need to be spaced out at a distance equal to your épaule width and for a close grip at a distance smaller than your épaule width.
3. As you have both arms extended in front of you holding the bar at the chosen grip width, bring your torse back around 30 degrees or so while creating a curvature on your lower back and sticking your poitrine out. C''est votre position de départ.
4. As you Expirez, bring the bar down until it touches your upper poitrine by drawing the épaules and the upper arms down and back. Conseil : Concentrate on squeezing the back muscles once you reach the full contracted position. The upper torse should remain stationary and only the arms should move. The forearms should do no other work except for holding the bar; therefore do not try to pull down the bar using the forearms.
5. After a second at the contracted position squeezing your omoplates together, Lentement, raise the bar back to the position de départ when vos bras are fully extended and the lats are fully stretched. Inspirez during this portion of le mouvement.
6. Répétez this motion for the prescribed amount of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Milieu du dos, Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Wide-Grip_Lat_Pulldown/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Wide-Grip Pulldown Behind The Neck', 'Dos', 'Poulie', '1. Sit down on a pull-down machine with a wide bar attached to the top pulley. Make sure that you adjust the genou pad of the machine to fit your height. These pads will prevent votre corps from being raised by the resistance attached to the bar.
2. Grab the bar with the paumes vers l''avant using the prescribed grip. Note on grips: For a prise large, vos mains need to be spaced out at a distance wider than your épaule width. For a prise moyenne, vos mains need to be spaced out at a distance equal to your épaule width and for a close grip at a distance smaller than your épaule width.
3. As you have both arms extended in front of you holding the bar at the chosen grip width, bring your torse and head forward. Think of an imaginary line from the center of the bar down to the back of your neck. C''est votre position de départ.
4. As you Expirez, bring the bar down until it touches the back of your neck by drawing the épaules and the upper arms down and back. Conseil : Concentrate on squeezing the back muscles once you reach the full contracted position. The upper torse should remain stationary and only the arms should move. The forearms should do no other work except for holding the bar; therefore do not try to pull down the bar using the forearms.
5. After a second on the contracted position squeezing your omoplates together, Lentement, raise the bar back to the position de départ when vos bras are fully extended and the lats are fully stretched. Inspirez during this portion of le mouvement.
6. Répétez this motion for the prescribed amount of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Milieu du dos, Épaules. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Wide-Grip_Pulldown_Behind_The_Neck/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Wide-Grip Rear Pull-Up', 'Dos', 'Poids de corps', '1. Grab the pull-up bar with the paumes vers l''avant using a prise large.
2. As you have both arms extended in front of you holding the bar, bring your torse forward and head so that there is an imaginary line from the pull-up bar to the back of your neck. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Pull your torse up until the bar is near the back of your neck. To do this, draw the épaules and upper arms down and back while slightly leaning votre tête forward. Expirez as you perform this portion of le mouvement. Conseil : Concentrate on squeezing the back muscles once you reach the full contracted position. The upper torse should remain stationary as it moves through space and only the arms should move. The forearms should do no other work other than hold the bar.
4. After a second on the contracted position, start to inspirez and Lentement, lower your torse back to the position de départ when vos bras are fully extended and the lats are fully stretched.
5. Répétez this motion for the prescribed amount of repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Biceps, Milieu du dos, Épaules. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Wide-Grip_Rear_Pull-Up/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Wide-Grip Standing Barbell Curl', 'Biceps', 'Barre', '1. Tenez-vous debout avec your torse upright while holding a barre at the wide outer handle. The palm of vos mains should be facing forward. The coudes should be close to the torse. C''est votre position de départ.
2. While holding the upper arms stationary, curl the poids forward while contracting the biceps as you Expirez. Conseil : Only the forearms should move.
3. Continue le mouvement until your biceps are entièrement contracté and the bar is at épaule level. Maintenez la position 1 seconde and squeeze the biceps hard.
4. Lentement, begin to bring the bar back to position de départ as your Inspirez.
5. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Wide-Grip_Standing_Barbell_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Wide Stance Barbell Squat', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. cet exercice is best performed inside a squat rack for safety purposes. To begin, first set the bar on a rack that best matches your height. Once the correct height is chosen and the bar is loaded, step under the bar and place the back of your épaules (slightly below the neck) across it.
2. Hold on to the bar using both arms at each side and lift it off the rack by first pushing with vos jambes and at the same time straightening your torse.
3. Step away from the rack and position vos jambes using a wider-than-épaule-width stance with the toes slightly pointed out. Keep votre tête up en permanence as looking down will get you off balance, and also maintain a straight back. C''est votre position de départ.
4. Begin to Lentement, lower the bar by bending the genous as you maintain a straight posture with the head up. Continue down until the angle between the upper leg and the mollets becomes slightly less than 90-degrees (which is the point in which the upper legs are below parallèle au sol). Inspirez as you perform this portion of le mouvement. Conseil : If you performed the exercise correctly, the front of the genous should make an imaginary straight line with the toes that is perpendiculaire à the front. If your genous are past that imaginary line (if they are past your toes) then you are placing undue stress on the genou and the exercise has been performed incorrectly.
5. Begin to raise the bar as you expirez by pushing le sol with the heel of your foot as you straighten the legs again and go back to the position de départ.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Wide_Stance_Barbell_Squat/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Wide Stance Stiff Legs', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Barre', '1. Begin with a barre loaded on le sol. Adopt a wide stance, and then bend at the hanches to grab the bar. Your hanches should be as far back as possible, and vos jambes nearly straight. Keep votre dos straight, and votre tête and poitrine up. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Begin le mouvement be engaging the hanches, driving them forward as you allow the arms to hang straight. Continue until you are standing straight up, and then Lentement, return the poids to the position de départ. For successive reps, the poids need not touch le sol.', 'Muscles secondaires : Adducteurs, Fessiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Wide_Stance_Stiff_Legs/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Wind Sprints', 'Abdominaux', 'Poids de corps', '1. Hang from a pull-up bar using a pronated grip. vos bras and legs should be extended. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Begin by quickly raising one genou as high as you can. Do not swing votre corps or vos jambes. 3
3. Immediately reverse the motion, returning that leg to the position de départ. Simultaneously raise the opposite genou as high as possible.
4. Continue alternating between legs until the set is complete.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Wind_Sprints/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Windmills', 'Abducteurs', 'Autre', '1. Allongez-vous au sol with vos bras extended out to the sides and vos jambes straight. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Lift one leg and quickly cross it over votre corps, attempting to touch the ground near the opposite hand.
3. Revenez en position de départ, and Répétez with the opposite leg. Continue to alternate for 10-20 repetitions.', 'Muscles secondaires : Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Windmills/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('World''s Greatest Stretch', 'Ischio-jambiers', 'Autre', '1. This is a three-part stretch. Begin by lunging forward, with your front foot flat on the ground and on the toes of votre dos foot. With your genous bent, squat down until your genou is almost touching the ground. Keep your torse erect, and hold this position for 10-20 seconds.
2. Now, place the arm on the same side as your front leg on the ground, with the coude next to the foot. Your other hand should be placed on the ground, parallel to your lead leg, to help support you during this portion of the stretch.
3. After 10-20 seconds, place vos mains on either side of your front foot. Raise the toes of the front foot off of the ground, and straighten your leg. You may need to reposition your rear leg to do so. Maintenez 10-20 secondes, and then Répétez the entire sequence for the other side.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Quadriceps. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Worlds_Greatest_Stretch/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Wrist Circles', 'Avant-bras', 'Poids de corps', '1. Start by standing straight with vos pieds being épaule width apart from each other. Elevate vos bras to the side of you until they are fully extended and parallèle au sol at a height that is evenly aligned with your épaules. Conseil : Your torse and arms should form the letter "T: Your palms should be facing down. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Keeping your entire body stationary except for the poignets, begin to rotate both poignets forward in a circular motion. Conseil : Pretend that you are trying to draw circles by using vos mains as the brush. Breathe normally as you perform cet exercice.
3. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Wrist_Circles/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Wrist Roller', 'Avant-bras', 'Autre', '1. To begin, stand straight up grabbing a poignet roller using a pronated grip (paumes vers down). vos pieds should be épaule width apart.
2. Lentement, lift both arms until they are fully extended and parallèle au sol in front of you. Note: Make sure the rope is not wrapped around the roller. Your entire body should be stationary except for the forearms. C''est votre position de départ.
3. Rotate one poignet at a time in an upward motion to bring the poids up to the bar by rolling the rope around the roller.
4. Once the poids has reached the bar, Lentement, begin to lower the poids back down by rotating the poignet in a downward motion until the poids reaches the position de départ.
5. Répétez for the prescribed amount of repetitions in your program.', 'Muscles secondaires : Épaules. Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Wrist_Roller/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Wrist Rotations with Straight Bar', 'Avant-bras', 'Barre', '1. Hold a barre with both hands and your paumes vers down; hands spaced about épaule width. C''est votre position de départ.
2. Alternating between each of vos mains, perform le mouvement by extending the poignet as though you were rolling up a newspaper. Continue alternating back and forth until failure.
3. Reverse the motion by flexing the poignet, rolling the opposite direction. Continue the alternating motion until failure.', 'Niveau : Débutant.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Wrist_Rotations_with_Straight_Bar/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Yoke Walk', 'Quadriceps', 'Autre', '1. The yoke is usually done with a yoke apparatus, but is sometimes seen with refrigerators or other heavy objects.
2. Begin by racking the apparatus across the back of the épaules. With votre tête looking forward and back arched, lift the yoke by driving through the heels.
3. Begin walking as quickly as possible using short, quick steps. You may hold the side posts of the yoke to help steady it and hold it in position. Continue for the given distance as fast as possible, usually 75-100 feet.', 'Muscles secondaires : Abdominaux, Abducteurs, Adducteurs, Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers, Bas du dos. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Yoke_Walk/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Zercher Squats', 'Quadriceps', 'Barre', '1. cet exercice is best performed inside a squat rack for safety purposes. To begin, first set the bar on a rack that best matches your height. The correct height should be anywhere above the waist but below the poitrine. Once the correct height is chosen and the bar is loaded, lock vos mains together and place the bar on top of vos bras in between the forearm and upper arm.
2. Lift the bar up so that it is resting on top of your forearms. If you are holding the bar properly, it should look as if you have vos bras crossed but with a bar running across them.
3. Step away from the rack and position vos jambes using a épaule width medium stance with the toes slightly pointed out. Keep votre tête up en permanence as looking down will get you off balance and also maintain a straight back. C''est votre position de départ. (Note: For the purposes of this discussion we will use the medium stance described above which targets overall development; however you can choose any of the three stances discussed in the foot stances section).
4. Begin to lower the bar by bending the genous as you maintain a straight posture with the head up. Continue down until the angle between the upper leg and the mollets becomes slightly less than 90-degrees (which is the point in which the upper legs are below parallèle au sol). Inspirez as you perform this portion of le mouvement. Conseil : If you performed the exercise correctly, the front of the genous should make an imaginary straight line with the toes that is perpendiculaire à the front. If your genous are past that imaginary line (if they are past your toes) then you are placing undue stress on the genou and the exercise has been performed incorrectly.
5. Begin to raise the bar as you expirez by pushing le sol with the ball of your foot mainly as you straighten the legs again and go back to the position de départ.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Mollets, Fessiers, Ischio-jambiers. Niveau : Avancé.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Zercher_Squats/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Zottman Curl', 'Biceps', 'Haltères', '1. Tenez-vous debout avec your torse upright and a haltère in each hand being held bras tendus. The coudes should be close to the torse.
2. Make sure the palms of the hands are facing each other. C''est votre position de départ.
3. While holding the upper arm stationary, curl the poids while contracting the biceps as you Expirez. Only the forearms should move. Your poignet should rotate so that you have a supinated (palms up) grip. Continue le mouvement until your biceps are entièrement contracté and the haltères are at épaule level.
4. Maintenez la position 1 seconde as you squeeze the biceps.
5. Now during the contracted position, rotate your poignet until you now have a pronated (paumes vers down) grip with the thumb at a higher position than the pinky.
6. Lentement, begin to bring the haltères back down using the pronated grip.
7. As the haltères close your cuisses, start rotating the poignet so that you go back to a neutral (paumes vers votre corps) grip.
8. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Zottman_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.exercises (name, muscle_group, equipment, description, tips, gif_url) VALUES ('Zottman Preacher Curl', 'Biceps', 'Haltères', '1. Grab a haltère in each hand and place your upper arms on top of the preacher banc or the incline banc. The haltères should be held at épaule height and the coudes should be flexed. Hold the haltères with the palms of vos mains facing down. C''est votre position de départ.
2. As you Inspirez, Lentement, lower the haltères keeping the palms down until your upper arm is extended and your biceps are fully stretched.
3. Now rotate your poignets once you are at the bottom of le mouvement so that the palms of the hands are facing up.
4. As you expirez, use your biceps to curl the poids up until they are entièrement contracté and the haltères are at épaule height. Again, remember that to ensure full contraction you need to bring that small finger higher than the thumb.
5. Squeeze the biceps hard for a second at the contracted position and rotate your poignets so that the palms are facing down again.
6. Répétez selon le nombre de répétitions souhaité.', 'Muscles secondaires : Avant-bras. Niveau : Intermédiaire.', 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yuhonas/free-exercise-db/main/exercises/Zottman_Preacher_Curl/0.jpg') ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
